pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% INTEGRATION-TEST: lenient-header-counts
% The positive companion of
% `incorrect/version3/cnf_under_declared_variable_index`: what
% `--lenient-header-counts` exists for must keep working.
%
% This file's `p cnf 1 1` header is wrong about both counts -- it declares one
% variable and one clause where the file has two clauses over variable 5 -- and
% that is precisely the case the flag is for: a DIMACS file whose padded or
% stale header disagrees with its contents is still a formula, and a proof
% against it is still checkable. The formula is `(x5) AND (~x5)`, which really
% is unsatisfiable, so this proof must verify.
%
% It is also the exact spelling that used to read out of bounds while returning
% the right verdict by accident, which is why it is pinned as an accept rather
% than left to the reproducer that shows the wrong one: sizing the variable
% space from the file's contents has to keep this verifying, and has to do so
% without the debug assertion in `Assignment::get_lit_value_unchecked` firing.
f 2;
rup >= 1;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT : -1;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
